course: dictionary
lesson: 8008
title: Redwood: a record-breaking tree
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A redwood is a very tall tree. You can work this out from the words around it. «Coast redwoods in California are the tallest trees in the world» tells you the redwood is a tree, and that it grows very tall.
explain: «Stand at the foot of a coast redwood in California and the people beside you look like ants.» The foot of a tree is its bottom, so you are standing at the base of its trunk, and the tree is so huge that people look tiny.
explain: Redwood can also mean the wood itself. Check by swapping in your meaning: «The table was made of redwood» means the table was made of reddish wood from these trees. Phrases such as redwood forest and giant redwood help too.
fact: A redwood is a very tall evergreen tree with reddish bark, found mainly in California.
fact: Coast redwoods are the tallest trees on Earth.
fact: «Hyperion» is a redwood about 116 metres tall, taller than the Statue of Liberty with its base.
fact: Redwood can also mean the reddish wood from these trees; the wood is uncountable, so you say some redwood, not a redwood.
exercise: «Stand at the foot of a coast redwood.» What is the foot of a tree? | The top of its leaves | Its shadow | Its bark | *The bottom of its trunk
exercise: Where do redwoods grow mainly? | In the middle of the sea | In the Sahara desert | *In California | On the Moon
exercise: «Hyperion is a redwood about 116 metres tall.» What is Hyperion? | A bird that lives in the forest | A bright red colour | *A very tall tree | A country in Europe
test: «Some redwoods are over 2,000 years old.» What does this tell us? | *They are record-breakers, very old and very tall | They lose all their leaves every autumn | They are small bushes that grow in gardens
test: «The table was made of redwood.» What does redwood mean here? | *The reddish wood from redwood trees | A forest in Asia | A tree in a park | A red painted table
exam: In «Coast redwoods in California are the tallest trees in the world», which words tell you redwood is a tree? | coast | world | California | *tallest trees
